Viewer discretion is advised.]

6
00:00:10,020 --> 00:00:11,550
For this MV...

7
00:00:11,570 --> 00:00:13,550
you'll be the director once again, Jaab.

8
00:00:13,570 --> 00:00:15,160
The mood of the song is very sad,

9
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:16,960
so I want somewhere that feels

10
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:17,760
lonely and isolated.

11
00:00:17,780 --> 00:00:18,840
You can visit my house.

12
00:00:18,980 --> 00:00:19,440
Huh?!

13
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:21,260
My house there has a lot of isolated corners.

14
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:23,160
Can I really go there?

15
00:00:24,980 --> 00:00:26,770
Your hair is too long.

16
00:00:26,790 --> 00:00:29,620
It was getting in your eyes,
so I wanted to brush it away.

17
00:00:29,660 --> 00:00:31,590
Why would that bother you?

18
00:00:31,610 --> 00:00:33,520
It did bother me,
because I was looking...

19
00:01:29,030 --> 00:01:29,850
Jane.

20
00:01:30,490 --> 00:01:32,620
I'm too scared to scrub it any harder.

21
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:34,900
I'm afraid your skin might come off.

22
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:39,930
Brats,

23
00:01:39,950 --> 00:01:41,720
both you and the marker.

24
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:45,410
Fine, fine.

25
00:01:45,740 --> 00:01:47,110
I guess I'm a brat, then.

26
00:01:50,890 --> 00:01:52,040
Cut it out already, Jane.

27
00:01:52,060 --> 00:01:53,120
You'll scrape yourself.

28
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:57,000
How do I get home unnoticed now?

29
00:01:58,890 --> 00:01:59,760
You'll be fine.

30
00:01:59,860 --> 00:02:00,720
Trust me,

31
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:02,530
no one actually cares that much.

32
00:02:04,050 --> 00:02:04,860
Mm.

33
00:02:08,890 --> 00:02:09,510
How about...

34
00:02:09,850 --> 00:02:10,720
you wear a face mask?

35
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:12,720
Here.

36
00:02:13,710 --> 00:02:14,990
The mark is on my forehead.

37
00:02:15,010 --> 00:02:16,560
How would this help, Jaab?

38
00:02:19,530 --> 00:02:21,150
It definitely helps, Jane!

39
00:02:21,170 --> 00:02:22,120
Put it on like this.

40
00:02:22,620 --> 00:02:23,360
See?

41
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:25,760
There! How about that, Jane?

42
00:02:25,780 --> 00:02:27,320
With this, I assure you.

43
00:02:27,340 --> 00:02:28,370
No one will see it

44
00:02:28,390 --> 00:02:29,560
for sure.

45
00:02:30,260 --> 00:02:31,280
Ow, Jane!

46
00:02:33,100 --> 00:02:34,280
That hurt.

47
00:02:45,710 --> 00:02:46,360
Jane.

48
00:02:48,230 --> 00:02:48,820
Here.

49
00:02:48,840 --> 00:02:49,660
For you.

50
00:02:56,680 --> 00:02:57,750
I don't need it.

51
00:02:59,190 --> 00:03:00,080
Oh, why not?

52
00:03:00,410 --> 00:03:01,860
Wear it, Jane.

53
00:03:03,380 --> 00:03:04,770
It smells really nice, and...

54
00:03:04,790 --> 00:03:06,680
it's got a hood to hide
that forehead of yours.

55
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:07,940
Take it.

56
00:03:08,130 --> 00:03:09,040
It smells very nice.

57
00:03:25,020 --> 00:03:25,680
Ow! Jeez...

58
00:03:26,070 --> 00:03:26,640
Ow...

59
00:03:26,730 --> 00:03:27,470
It's you

60
00:03:27,510 --> 00:03:28,220
who has a big forehead.

61
00:03:28,590 --> 00:03:29,350
Come on.

62
00:03:31,500 --> 00:03:32,390
Wait, Jane.

63
00:03:32,580 --> 00:03:33,200
What are you doing?

64
00:03:33,420 --> 00:03:34,080
I'm changing, obviously.

65
00:03:34,200 --> 00:03:35,320
Go change in the bathroom.

66
00:03:35,420 --> 00:03:36,360
You can't do it here.

67
00:03:36,460 --> 00:03:38,040
It's fine. Nobody is around.

68
00:03:38,060 --> 00:03:38,890
But I'm here!

69
00:03:38,910 --> 00:03:40,060
It's okay. I don't mind.

70
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:41,940
But I do mind, Jane! Please!

71
00:03:41,960 --> 00:03:43,500
- It's okay, Jaab.
- No, don't! No, Jane!

72
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:45,220
- Please don't, Jane.
- So we can finally head home.

73
00:03:45,240 --> 00:03:46,500
Go change in the bathroom, please.

74
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:47,360
- Jane!
- Jaab!

75
00:03:47,380 --> 00:03:47,960
No!

76
00:03:48,110 --> 00:03:49,080
I can see everything!

77
00:03:49,100 --> 00:03:50,060
Ah, Jane! I can see everything!

78
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:51,560
Jane!!

79
00:03:53,240 --> 00:03:55,020
So much for a forehead makeover.

80
00:04:16,480 --> 00:04:19,440
This brat would like to say sorry. Forgive me.

81
00:04:23,190 --> 00:04:26,460
Once again,
the chemistry between us grows stronger

82
00:04:26,920 --> 00:04:28,630
to the point where it triggers a reaction

83
00:04:28,660 --> 00:04:31,500
that makes my heart feel like it might burst.

84
00:06:21,380 --> 00:06:22,990
I think I've settled in.

85
00:06:25,830 --> 00:06:28,240
Has anyone been picking on you
at the new company?

86
00:06:28,530 --> 00:06:29,680
New?

87
00:06:29,700 --> 00:06:31,280
I've been working here for months now.

88
00:06:31,300 --> 00:06:32,440
It's been almost a year already.

89
00:06:33,880 --> 00:06:36,000
Right. I forgot.

90
00:06:36,340 --> 00:06:39,640
It feels like you just left yesterday.

91
00:06:39,890 --> 00:06:41,130
Min, don't be so dramatic.

92
00:06:41,150 --> 00:06:42,250
I'm a grown-up, okay?

93
00:06:43,900 --> 00:06:46,840
So, has anyone been picking on you?

94
00:06:47,290 --> 00:06:48,200
I don't think so.

95
00:06:51,730 --> 00:06:56,090
And, like...
has anyone been hitting on you?

96
00:07:01,450 --> 00:07:02,390
Maybe.

97
00:07:04,920 --> 00:07:05,570
Whoa...

98
00:07:05,590 --> 00:07:07,170
I think they need to get a new coach, Khanoon.

99
00:07:07,190 --> 00:07:07,840
Yeah.

100
00:07:07,860 --> 00:07:09,500
They're screwed if they don't.

101
00:07:09,520 --> 00:07:10,280
Watching them is a waste of time.

102
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:12,000
I couldn't fucking sleep at all. Damn it.

103
00:07:15,520 --> 00:07:16,460
Sheesh.

104
00:07:16,480 --> 00:07:18,400
So, our sweet manager

105
00:07:18,420 --> 00:07:20,120
clocks in early today?

106
00:07:20,170 --> 00:07:20,840
Look.

107
00:07:20,860 --> 00:07:23,190
These mangoes from Jane's garden house

108
00:07:23,210 --> 00:07:24,010
taste wonderful!

109
00:07:24,030 --> 00:07:24,760
Here. Try some.

110
00:07:26,940 --> 00:07:27,650
Hm!

111
00:07:27,670 --> 00:07:28,500
How is it?

112
00:07:28,930 --> 00:07:30,280
It's really good!

113
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:33,040
Told you.

114
00:07:34,430 --> 00:07:35,340
And...

115
00:07:35,570 --> 00:07:37,520
Will I get to eat a fresh one tomorrow?

116
00:07:38,010 --> 00:07:38,580
Yeah.

117
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:39,560
Whoa, really?!

118
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:40,910
Is there anything else

119
00:07:40,930 --> 00:07:42,200
that I can try at your orchard?

120
00:07:43,360 --> 00:07:44,280
It's packed.

121
00:07:44,660 --> 00:07:45,460
Whoa...

122
00:07:45,530 --> 00:07:46,240
Hey,

123
00:07:46,310 --> 00:07:46,970
Jaab.

124
00:07:47,090 --> 00:07:49,910
I heard that you'll be looking for
inspirations at Jane's garden house?

125
00:07:51,090 --> 00:07:52,380
Yes, Sis.

126
00:07:52,400 --> 00:07:53,890
Marvelous!

127
00:07:53,910 --> 00:07:55,400
He's helping us cut costs.

128
00:07:55,740 --> 00:07:57,650
- You're such a sweetheart.
- Whoa, Sis...

129
00:07:58,130 --> 00:07:59,760
Please put the knife down first,

130
00:08:01,950 --> 00:08:02,720
or else

131
00:08:02,880 --> 00:08:05,320
you'll end up nicking this handsome face.

132
00:08:06,450 --> 00:08:07,400
Right!

133
00:08:09,820 --> 00:08:10,370
Hey.

134
00:08:10,650 --> 00:08:12,470
Are you helping the company save money

135
00:08:12,490 --> 00:08:14,470
or are you supporting
someone's business here?

136
00:08:14,640 --> 00:08:16,180
Damn you, Khanoon...

137
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:16,720
Jaab.

138
00:08:16,790 --> 00:08:17,560
Yes? What is it?

139
00:08:19,890 --> 00:08:21,120
Sheesh...

140
00:08:21,430 --> 00:08:23,720
Your voice is softer.

141
00:08:25,550 --> 00:08:27,240
I think you're probably hungry.

142
00:08:28,660 --> 00:08:30,650
If you can't shut up, just eat this.

143
00:08:30,670 --> 00:08:31,480
- There!
- What the hell?

144
00:08:33,280 --> 00:08:33,890
Uh...

145
00:08:34,180 --> 00:08:35,740
Your hoodie isn't completely dry yet.

146
00:08:35,760 --> 00:08:36,660
Do you need it tomorrow?

147
00:08:36,680 --> 00:08:37,840
I'll put it in my luggage.

148
00:08:38,240 --> 00:08:39,310
It's fine, Jane.

149
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:40,360
I've got a couple more.

150
00:08:40,420 --> 00:08:42,040
I don't want to take up your space.

151
00:08:43,020 --> 00:08:44,560
It'll be cold at night, though.

152
00:08:45,020 --> 00:08:46,640
Bring some warm clothes
to keep you cozy.

153
00:08:47,020 --> 00:08:47,600
Okay.

154
00:08:47,940 --> 00:08:48,980
Got it.

155
00:08:49,250 --> 00:08:49,970
By the way...

156
00:08:49,990 --> 00:08:51,920
when do you want me to
pick you up tomorrow?

157
00:08:52,550 --> 00:08:53,660
Around 7-8 A.M., maybe?

158
00:08:53,680 --> 00:08:54,960
We'll arrive there at noon.

159
00:08:56,380 --> 00:08:56,960
Okay.

160
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:01,840
Don't forget to pick me up, too.

161
00:09:04,080 --> 00:09:05,170
Wasn't the sticky rice enough?

162
00:09:05,190 --> 00:09:06,040
Shut it!

163
00:09:06,580 --> 00:09:07,550
You ruined the moment.

164
00:09:10,980 --> 00:09:12,480
These mangoes are super yummy.

165
00:09:12,550 --> 00:09:13,920
Bring me some more, if you don't mind.

166
00:09:13,940 --> 00:09:15,340
- Sure thing.
- I want my parents to enjoy them, too.

167
00:09:15,360 --> 00:09:17,040
- Sure.
- They like mangoes.

168
00:09:17,060 --> 00:09:17,890
Hey.

169
00:09:17,910 --> 00:09:19,130
I'm first.

170
00:09:19,150 --> 00:09:20,120
I'm first in line.

171
00:09:29,940 --> 00:09:31,000
Whoa, what?!

172
00:09:31,020 --> 00:09:32,120
Whoa, Jaab!

173
00:09:32,240 --> 00:09:34,490
What the hell is wrong with you?
Why did you take me here?

174
00:09:34,510 --> 00:09:35,480
Let go! What is it?

175
00:09:35,790 --> 00:09:36,720
What the hell are you doing?

176
00:09:36,870 --> 00:09:38,160
Tell me what you know.

177
00:09:39,740 --> 00:09:40,320
Know what?

178
00:09:40,380 --> 00:09:41,720
You're acting like you do.

179
00:09:41,810 --> 00:09:43,440
Tell me what I know, then!

180
00:09:43,560 --> 00:09:45,640
Don't even try to trick me, asshole.

181
00:09:45,760 --> 00:09:47,580
What the hell are you talking about, exactly?

182
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:48,480
Asshole?

183
00:09:49,590 --> 00:09:50,780
It's Jane.

184
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:51,480
I mean...

185
00:09:51,610 --> 00:09:52,920
I'm talking about Jane.

186
00:09:53,390 --> 00:09:54,720
Oh...

187
00:09:55,100 --> 00:09:56,640
Jane...

188
00:09:57,320 --> 00:09:57,960
What about him?

189
00:09:58,620 --> 00:10:00,040
Uh, well...

190
00:10:02,080 --> 00:10:04,430
It's about me going to his place...

191
00:10:04,740 --> 00:10:07,020
He invited me himself,
so don't take it the wrong way.

192
00:10:07,060 --> 00:10:07,860
Jane's house

193
00:10:07,880 --> 00:10:09,540
has a massive orchard

194
00:10:09,560 --> 00:10:10,660
and tons of hills.

195
00:10:10,680 --> 00:10:13,300
And people can visit and walk around.

196
00:10:13,320 --> 00:10:14,800
It's not just the two of us.

197
00:10:15,230 --> 00:10:18,020
Oh... I see.

198
00:10:18,040 --> 00:10:19,520
- Mm.
- And?

199
00:10:20,520 --> 00:10:21,120
And...

200
00:10:21,760 --> 00:10:22,560
And...

201
00:10:23,790 --> 00:10:25,860
The reason I speak more softly around Jane

202
00:10:25,880 --> 00:10:27,020
is because he's small.

203
00:10:27,040 --> 00:10:29,380
I don't want to be loud and startle him.

204
00:10:29,400 --> 00:10:30,250
Small?

205
00:10:30,620 --> 00:10:31,990
He's only this tiny.

206
00:10:32,200 --> 00:10:33,360
The size of a bottle?

207
00:10:35,140 --> 00:10:35,780
He's like...

208
00:10:35,800 --> 00:10:37,220
- He's only this tiny, you see.
- Oh.

209
00:10:37,240 --> 00:10:37,920
- Like...
- This tiny?

210
00:10:38,400 --> 00:10:40,120
And his eyes twinkle.

211
00:10:40,330 --> 00:10:41,500
When he smiles...

212
00:10:41,630 --> 00:10:42,640
he smiles broadly

213
00:10:43,030 --> 00:10:44,400
almost from ear to ear.

214
00:10:44,750 --> 00:10:45,440
Also...

215
00:10:45,600 --> 00:10:47,670
his teeth are perfectly aligned.

216
00:10:47,690 --> 00:10:48,350
Seeing them makes me...

217
00:10:48,370 --> 00:10:50,540
want to see him every morning.

218
00:10:50,560 --> 00:10:51,520
Do you like Jane?

219
00:10:54,240 --> 00:10:55,020
I...

220
00:10:55,880 --> 00:10:56,560
like Jane...

221
00:10:58,430 --> 00:10:59,280
Right?

222
00:11:02,800 --> 00:11:03,640
Do I?

223
00:11:06,240 --> 00:11:07,440
How would I know?

224
00:11:08,340 --> 00:11:10,160
What should I do, Khanoon?

225
00:11:10,520 --> 00:11:11,840
I've never felt this way.

226
00:11:13,640 --> 00:11:15,440
When you're sure about it,

227
00:11:15,640 --> 00:11:16,980
tell me later.

228
00:11:17,380 --> 00:11:19,320
And I'll help you out.

229
00:11:19,810 --> 00:11:21,030
I know that

230
00:11:21,290 --> 00:11:23,540
a clueless loser like you

231
00:11:23,560 --> 00:11:24,960
can't make a move on your own.

232
00:11:27,830 --> 00:11:28,760
What do I have to do, then?

233
00:11:29,570 --> 00:11:31,040
Be sure about it first.

234
00:11:31,150 --> 00:11:32,320
That's it. I'll get going now.

235
00:11:32,340 --> 00:11:33,040
Wait!

236
00:11:33,180 --> 00:11:33,790
See you.

237
00:11:33,810 --> 00:11:35,430
Talk to me when you're sure enough.

238
00:11:35,450 --> 00:11:36,270
Damn it!

239
00:11:39,720 --> 00:11:41,090
Do I really have a crush on Jane?

240
00:11:41,440 --> 00:11:42,700
Or do I just think that
he's adorable?

241
00:11:42,720 --> 00:11:44,600
Which means you have a crush on him, idiot!

242
00:11:44,910 --> 00:11:47,000
Let's go. I've got tons of
unfinished tasks to take care of.

243
00:11:47,020 --> 00:11:48,440
Not just me, but you as well.

244
00:11:48,910 --> 00:11:50,320
Right. I'll join you soon.

245
00:11:54,360 --> 00:11:55,760
Damn it, Jaab!

246
00:12:00,500 --> 00:12:01,940
Thinking that he's adorable
means I have a crush on him?

247
00:12:04,870 --> 00:12:05,770
Do I, though?

248
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:08,170
Somebody like me?

249
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:11,150
Come on, Jaab!

250
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:14,000
Gosh...

251
00:12:14,580 --> 00:12:16,160
Why the hell is this stuff so complicated?

252
00:12:23,370 --> 00:12:23,980
Oh.

253
00:12:24,990 --> 00:12:25,770
Mek?

254
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:27,010
What brings you here?

255
00:12:29,580 --> 00:12:30,650
Who's Jane?

256
00:12:35,790 --> 00:12:37,170
Whoa.

257
00:12:37,900 --> 00:12:39,650
Khanoon, you bastard.

258
00:12:39,670 --> 00:12:41,720
He can't keep a secret to save his life, huh?

259
00:12:42,210 --> 00:12:43,080
Come on, Jaab.

260
00:12:43,100 --> 00:12:44,960
Have you forgotten our group's motto?

261
00:12:45,030 --> 00:12:47,160
"Nothing is a personal matter,

262
00:12:47,330 --> 00:12:49,080
for it is always our matter."

263
00:12:49,350 --> 00:12:50,650
Yay!

264
00:12:51,800 --> 00:12:52,680
Yay...

265
00:12:54,710 --> 00:12:56,040
It's just the three of us.

266
00:12:56,400 --> 00:12:58,300
Can you even call that a group?

267
00:12:58,690 --> 00:12:59,660
For me,

268
00:12:59,680 --> 00:13:01,840
it's a group if there are
more than two people.

269
00:13:05,540 --> 00:13:06,760
Hey, hey, Mek.

270
00:13:06,810 --> 00:13:07,760
Hey, what the fuck are you doing?!

271
00:13:07,830 --> 00:13:08,630
Mek, give it to me!

272
00:13:08,650 --> 00:13:09,840
Mek, Mek, Mek.

273
00:13:09,920 --> 00:13:11,100
- You...
- Adorable.

274
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:11,720
Hey!

275
00:13:13,800 --> 00:13:15,200
Cut it out, damn it.

276
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:16,370
One picture, that's it.

277
00:13:17,260 --> 00:13:18,300
Become his boyfriend first

278
00:13:18,320 --> 00:13:19,540
before you get possessive, my guy.

279
00:13:19,560 --> 00:13:20,600
Don't jump the gun.

280
00:13:20,960 --> 00:13:21,700
His boyfriend?

281
00:13:25,310 --> 00:13:26,180
His boyfriend?

282
00:13:29,400 --> 00:13:31,760
You've lost it, just like what Khanoon told me.

283
00:13:33,410 --> 00:13:33,950
What?

284
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:35,720
And look at you.

285
00:13:36,070 --> 00:13:37,480
You didn't tell me that you were back.

286
00:13:43,380 --> 00:13:46,200
I took my dog to the vet nearby,
so I decided to swing by.

287
00:13:46,560 --> 00:13:48,080
Mon needs to be hospitalized.

288
00:13:49,870 --> 00:13:51,120
So you want to crash here for free?

289
00:13:51,710 --> 00:13:52,980
Come on.

290
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:55,720
Your place is close to
my dog's go-to hospital.

291
00:13:56,080 --> 00:13:57,680
It's for the sake of my dog, alright?

292
00:13:57,710 --> 00:13:59,530
I'm not crashing here for free, though.

293
00:13:59,970 --> 00:14:00,810
This is in exchange for...

294
00:14:00,840 --> 00:14:02,720
some relationship advice from me.

295
00:14:05,510 --> 00:14:06,480
Did I ask for it?

296
00:14:09,490 --> 00:14:10,800
But I'm actually surprised that

297
00:14:10,990 --> 00:14:12,560
a goofball like you

298
00:14:12,730 --> 00:14:14,860
is invested in a relationship.

299
00:14:14,880 --> 00:14:16,790
Invested, my ass.

300
00:14:17,150 --> 00:14:18,120
I just...

301
00:14:18,810 --> 00:14:19,690
Just what?

302
00:14:20,990 --> 00:14:21,920
My heart just...

303
00:14:22,990 --> 00:14:23,920
quivers a little.

304
00:14:23,950 --> 00:14:25,640
Quivers a little?

305
00:14:25,660 --> 00:14:27,100
But you're about to haul your ass

306
00:14:27,120 --> 00:14:29,360
out of the city to stay at his house?

307
00:14:30,150 --> 00:14:31,000
Yeah!

308
00:14:31,150 --> 00:14:32,240
But I have a reason for it.

309
00:14:32,400 --> 00:14:33,520
I'm heading there for work.

310
00:14:33,680 --> 00:14:35,080
And I'm warning you.

311
00:14:35,510 --> 00:14:37,080
What you heard from Khanoon

312
00:14:37,110 --> 00:14:38,600
needs to be taken with a grain of salt.

313
00:14:39,820 --> 00:14:41,360
You don't need to remind me.

314
00:14:41,380 --> 00:14:42,480
I took it with a grain of salt,

315
00:14:42,610 --> 00:14:44,110
but I can see hearts

316
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:45,440
in your eyes.

317
00:14:45,550 --> 00:14:46,100
Wait...

318
00:14:49,960 --> 00:14:50,980
You're talking nonsense.

319
00:14:53,040 --> 00:14:54,060
Love

320
00:14:54,080 --> 00:14:55,640
isn't that intimidating.

321
00:14:55,750 --> 00:14:56,720
Trust me.

322
00:14:58,840 --> 00:15:00,760
I'm too scared to think about it.

323
00:15:02,110 --> 00:15:03,160
Give it a try.

324
00:15:13,510 --> 00:15:15,860
Khanoon said you're heading to
Jane's place tomorrow, right?

325
00:15:15,880 --> 00:15:16,570
Yeah.

326
00:15:17,040 --> 00:15:18,840
Jane said it'd be cold at night,

327
00:15:19,010 --> 00:15:20,970
so I'm preparing some warm clothes.

328
00:15:26,080 --> 00:15:28,180
You told me to bring some warm clothes,

329
00:15:28,970 --> 00:15:30,670
but now you're shivering yourself?

330
00:15:35,110 --> 00:15:36,310
And...

331
00:15:37,720 --> 00:15:39,920
Would it keep me warm if I hugged you?

332
00:15:52,470 --> 00:15:53,320
How is it?

333
00:15:54,290 --> 00:15:55,950
Is the jacket as warm as me?

334
00:16:06,070 --> 00:16:07,650
Does Jane live near the North Pole or what?

335
00:16:10,900 --> 00:16:11,840
What do you mean?!

336
00:16:13,220 --> 00:16:14,600
North Pole, my ass.

337
00:16:15,430 --> 00:16:17,120
You said you'd go to his place,

338
00:16:17,150 --> 00:16:19,240
then you took out a down jacket.

339
00:16:19,290 --> 00:16:21,120
I thought it would be
snowing there or something.

340
00:16:24,160 --> 00:16:24,690
Well...

341
00:16:25,390 --> 00:16:26,840
It's in Phetchabun.

342
00:16:27,290 --> 00:16:29,960
And you're wearing a down jacket there?

343
00:16:32,030 --> 00:16:32,990
None of your business.

344
00:16:35,760 --> 00:16:37,810
Has love destroyed your IQ, my friend?

345
00:16:37,830 --> 00:16:38,390
Wait.

346
00:16:39,010 --> 00:16:40,510
This isn't my blazer.

347
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,290
It's fucking Jeng's.

348
00:16:42,490 --> 00:16:44,060
The maid must've taken the wrong one.

349
00:16:45,670 --> 00:16:46,290
Hey.

350
00:16:50,270 --> 00:16:51,160
How about you put it on?

351
00:16:51,630 --> 00:16:53,860
Try something new and make an impression.

352
00:17:01,340 --> 00:17:03,000
Jaab, you look absolutely stunning.

353
00:17:03,870 --> 00:17:05,830
You're too kind, Jane.

354
00:17:07,210 --> 00:17:08,080
Ready?

355
00:17:08,410 --> 00:17:09,000
Mm.

356
00:17:09,520 --> 00:17:10,160
Here.

357
00:17:10,440 --> 00:17:11,290
Alright, Jane!

358
00:17:11,350 --> 00:17:12,700
- That one, Jaab. There.
- Which one?

359
00:17:12,720 --> 00:17:14,320
Yes, get it. Come on.

360
00:17:14,340 --> 00:17:15,260
Yes, that one.

361
00:17:15,300 --> 00:17:16,230
This one, Jane?

362
00:17:16,250 --> 00:17:17,230
- Yes, that one.
- Okay.

363
00:17:17,250 --> 00:17:19,330
- Get it. Harder, harder. Come on.
- Just a moment.

364
00:17:19,350 --> 00:17:20,800
Great job, Jaab. You're amazing.

365
00:17:23,790 --> 00:17:24,680
Honestly,

366
00:17:24,950 --> 00:17:26,400
don't try to act tough.

367
00:17:27,040 --> 00:17:29,800
I know how badly
this trip messes with your heart.

368
00:17:33,060 --> 00:17:34,880
Will Jane know that I like him?

369
00:17:35,160 --> 00:17:37,200
If he finds out and hates me,

370
00:17:37,220 --> 00:17:38,200
what should I do?

371
00:17:39,320 --> 00:17:39,920
No.

372
00:17:40,140 --> 00:17:41,280
I do like him, don't I?

373
00:17:41,730 --> 00:17:42,720
I guess...

374
00:17:44,070 --> 00:17:44,960
Damn it, Jaab!

375
00:17:45,020 --> 00:17:46,600
Why did I fall for him?!

376
00:17:46,620 --> 00:17:48,190
Oh, my God! Damn it!

377
00:17:48,210 --> 00:17:49,320
Why...? Damn it!

378
00:17:49,340 --> 00:17:50,630
Why do I have feelings for him?!

379
00:17:53,160 --> 00:17:54,170
Mek, help me!

380
00:17:54,190 --> 00:17:55,490
Help me, damn it.

381
00:17:55,510 --> 00:17:57,830
Oh, my God!

382
00:18:05,630 --> 00:18:06,680
Did I keep you waiting?

383
00:18:06,700 --> 00:18:07,560
Oh, Jane.

384
00:18:09,870 --> 00:18:10,640
Whoa, Jane.

385
00:18:10,660 --> 00:18:11,970
Your bag is so small.

386
00:18:12,080 --> 00:18:14,150
I've got a ton of stuff on me.

387
00:18:14,170 --> 00:18:15,520
Mine looks so over-prepared.

388
00:18:15,610 --> 00:18:16,620
Not really.

389
00:18:17,240 --> 00:18:19,200
You're preparing to stay at another place.

390
00:18:19,290 --> 00:18:21,520
But that other place is my home.
My stuff is already there.

391
00:18:22,780 --> 00:18:23,720
Right, right, right.

392
00:18:23,880 --> 00:18:25,690
Give it to me. I'll load it in the trunk.

393
00:18:40,650 --> 00:18:41,920
Your bag...

394
00:18:42,140 --> 00:18:43,440
is just as tiny as you, isn't it?

395
00:18:44,870 --> 00:18:45,490
Mm.

396
00:18:46,420 --> 00:18:47,280
It's like...

397
00:18:47,650 --> 00:18:48,830
your pen.

398
00:18:49,370 --> 00:18:50,550
Your pen is a brat, just like you.

399
00:18:51,800 --> 00:18:53,400
Right at the start of this trip?

400
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:05,210
What are you waiting for? Come on.

401
00:19:07,030 --> 00:19:07,860
Jaab.

402
00:19:08,350 --> 00:19:10,040
You need to make it back here
in one piece, okay?

403
00:19:11,230 --> 00:19:12,270
Come on!

404
00:19:13,080 --> 00:19:13,830
Hurry.

405
00:19:24,360 --> 00:19:25,440
Jaab, have you eaten?

406
00:19:28,830 --> 00:19:31,360
That's a single serving,
so don't pretend like you care.

407
00:19:32,670 --> 00:19:33,260
Well, this.

408
00:19:33,750 --> 00:19:34,650
I made this one for you.

409
00:19:35,680 --> 00:19:36,320
Seriously?

410
00:19:37,220 --> 00:19:38,090
Fine, fine.

411
00:19:38,170 --> 00:19:39,290
Since you made it for me,

412
00:19:39,450 --> 00:19:40,160
I'll eat it.

413
00:19:42,890 --> 00:19:43,440
Here.

414
00:19:44,110 --> 00:19:45,120
Thank you.

415
00:19:47,490 --> 00:19:48,040
Hey!

416
00:19:48,060 --> 00:19:48,440
Whoa!

417
00:19:50,160 --> 00:19:51,380
Why did you hit me, Jane?

418
00:19:51,400 --> 00:19:53,560
You're driving. Why did you let go?

419
00:19:54,430 --> 00:19:55,720
It's on autopilot, Jane.

420
00:19:55,840 --> 00:19:57,110
It's a new feature.

421
00:19:57,240 --> 00:19:57,740
Cool, right?

422
00:19:57,760 --> 00:19:59,540
Dangerous. Don't do that again!

423
00:19:59,560 --> 00:20:01,920
It's a danger both to you
and to others on the road.

424
00:20:02,680 --> 00:20:03,830
Right.

425
00:20:04,150 --> 00:20:05,480
I won't do it again.

426
00:20:06,890 --> 00:20:08,520
Don't pull that face.

427
00:20:08,540 --> 00:20:10,280
I know that you haven't learned your lesson.

428
00:20:11,190 --> 00:20:12,400
Come on, Jane.

429
00:20:12,420 --> 00:20:13,610
What should I do, then?

430
00:20:14,120 --> 00:20:15,920
I can't let go,
so how am I supposed to eat?

431
00:20:18,070 --> 00:20:18,630
Here.

432
00:20:20,040 --> 00:20:20,590
Mm.

433
00:20:20,850 --> 00:20:22,200
This works, though.

434
00:20:28,780 --> 00:20:30,260
Oh, so good!

435
00:20:30,280 --> 00:20:31,000
Jaab.

436
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:33,160
- Chew before you talk.
- Chew before you talk.

437
00:20:34,690 --> 00:20:35,280
Mm.

438
00:20:35,620 --> 00:20:38,000
Do you need to choke to learn your lesson?

439
00:20:38,510 --> 00:20:40,590
"Do you need to choke to..."

440
00:20:44,230 --> 00:20:44,850
Jane.

441
00:20:46,540 --> 00:20:47,360
I'm choking.

442
00:20:48,940 --> 00:20:49,870
Thank you, Jane.

443
00:20:50,400 --> 00:20:51,200
Jane!

444
00:20:52,160 --> 00:20:53,600
Jane, I need water...

445
00:20:56,520 --> 00:20:57,280
Emergency.

446
00:20:57,320 --> 00:20:58,460
Help me, Jane!

447
00:20:59,340 --> 00:21:00,630
Jane!!

448
00:21:02,800 --> 00:21:03,950
Whoa, gentle, gentle.

449
00:21:03,970 --> 00:21:04,960
Gentle!

450
00:21:06,820 --> 00:21:07,660
Goodness...

451
00:21:09,080 --> 00:21:10,480
Were you that thirsty, dear?

452
00:21:10,520 --> 00:21:12,600
I'm sorry, Jane's mom...

453
00:21:13,690 --> 00:21:14,580
This is Auntie Kaew.

454
00:21:14,600 --> 00:21:15,320
She's my caretaker.

455
00:21:16,120 --> 00:21:17,630
I'm so sorry, Sis.

456
00:21:17,650 --> 00:21:18,560
I mean, Auntie.

457
00:21:20,470 --> 00:21:22,160
You might as well
tell me that tomorrow, Jane.

458
00:21:23,200 --> 00:21:25,600
My parents are taking care of
some business overseas.

459
00:21:25,860 --> 00:21:28,120
Oh, I was going to ask.

460
00:21:28,230 --> 00:21:30,720
You know that your parents
are away right now,

461
00:21:30,910 --> 00:21:32,120
so what brings you home?

462
00:21:32,470 --> 00:21:34,680
I know that nobody is here,

463
00:21:34,700 --> 00:21:36,280
so I want to keep you company.

464
00:21:37,100 --> 00:21:39,490
I don't want to be alone for too long.

465
00:21:40,080 --> 00:21:42,620
Aww...

466
00:21:42,710 --> 00:21:45,250
My boy is such a sweetheart.

467
00:21:45,270 --> 00:21:47,330
Why are you so, so sweet?

468
00:21:47,350 --> 00:21:49,000
Come here. Let me give you a smooch.

469
00:21:49,640 --> 00:21:50,440
Come here.

470
00:21:52,130 --> 00:21:54,740
Do you know how much
I missed you, Master Jane?

471
00:21:58,490 --> 00:22:01,260
Jaab, you're staying at this tiny house, okay?

472
00:22:04,050 --> 00:22:06,190
As you wish, Master Jane.

473
00:22:07,430 --> 00:22:08,920
I'm not as classy as you,
Master Attajiranont.

474
00:22:09,520 --> 00:22:10,680
Wait, hey...

475
00:22:10,870 --> 00:22:13,360
Have you been looking through
my family background or what?

476
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:15,020
Khanoon told me.

477
00:22:16,780 --> 00:22:18,050
What did he say?

478
00:22:18,070 --> 00:22:19,320
He said that

479
00:22:19,580 --> 00:22:21,640
your face doesn't match
your last name at all.

480
00:22:22,780 --> 00:22:24,520
So people don't believe
that you're rich.

481
00:22:29,930 --> 00:22:31,280
Is he taking a shot at me?

482
00:22:31,840 --> 00:22:33,960
Hey, Jane. Wait up!

483
00:22:34,060 --> 00:22:34,820
Jane!

484
00:22:35,550 --> 00:22:36,460
Wait for me.

485
00:22:41,210 --> 00:22:42,520
Whoa...

486
00:22:47,760 --> 00:22:48,920
Oh, Jane.

487
00:22:48,960 --> 00:22:50,280
Your place is stunning.

488
00:22:50,820 --> 00:22:52,480
I can tell a lot of work has gone into it.

489
00:22:53,230 --> 00:22:54,970
Dad designed everything himself.

490
00:22:55,400 --> 00:22:57,640
But it's mostly what Mom likes.

491
00:22:57,820 --> 00:22:59,920
Whoa, how romantic...

492
00:23:01,540 --> 00:23:02,970
The weather's really good here at night.

493
00:23:02,990 --> 00:23:05,280
I like sleeping here inside the mosquito net
with the windows open.

494
00:23:05,700 --> 00:23:07,580
But if this isn't up your alley,

495
00:23:08,720 --> 00:23:09,400
just turn the A/C on.

496
00:23:09,870 --> 00:23:10,660
Okay.

497
00:23:11,460 --> 00:23:12,120
Well then...

498
00:23:12,400 --> 00:23:13,490
do make yourself at home.

499
00:23:13,910 --> 00:23:15,550
Any spot here can be an isolated corner

500
00:23:15,570 --> 00:23:16,980
for your work.

501
00:23:17,220 --> 00:23:18,000
Don't hold back.

502
00:23:18,720 --> 00:23:19,580
Right.

503
00:23:32,180 --> 00:23:34,670
Had I met Jane back in my university days,

504
00:23:34,690 --> 00:23:38,840
I would've gotten a better grade in chemistry analysis.

505
00:23:39,620 --> 00:23:41,690
When it comes to
the chemistry between two people,

506
00:23:41,720 --> 00:23:45,180
not only does it make one's heart erupt,

507
00:23:45,360 --> 00:23:48,000
but it also turns something mundane

508
00:23:48,100 --> 00:23:50,800
into something extraordinarily special
like Mek said.

509
00:23:51,050 --> 00:23:53,120
I don't know if Jane feels the same,

510
00:23:55,040 --> 00:23:57,700
but I have to thank him
for making me feel this much.

511
00:24:04,200 --> 00:24:05,890
[SCENE 1: INT. GARDEN HOUSE - DAY]

512
00:24:05,910 --> 00:24:07,600
[CHARACTERS]

513
00:24:17,410 --> 00:24:18,210
Oh, oh.

514
00:24:19,260 --> 00:24:22,000
Why don't you rest
on the pillow, Master?

515
00:24:22,550 --> 00:24:24,750
I prefer your lap.

516
00:24:25,710 --> 00:24:26,900
Goodness!

517
00:24:27,380 --> 00:24:27,990
Oh,

518
00:24:28,560 --> 00:24:30,760
what has Bangkok done to my boy?

519
00:24:30,780 --> 00:24:31,480
Hm?

520
00:24:45,640 --> 00:24:47,710
That's what my seniors
at the company like to say,

521
00:24:47,730 --> 00:24:49,070
so I picked it up from them.

522
00:24:49,090 --> 00:24:50,750
Oh!

523
00:24:52,230 --> 00:24:54,570
What about your friend?

524
00:24:55,080 --> 00:24:56,650
What brings him here

525
00:24:56,670 --> 00:24:58,810
on the same trip?

526
00:25:00,580 --> 00:25:02,680
His name is Jaab.

527
00:25:04,280 --> 00:25:05,500
He's my colleague.

528
00:25:06,010 --> 00:25:07,250
We sit next to each other.

529
00:25:23,810 --> 00:25:25,480
Jaab is big and tall.

530
00:25:26,560 --> 00:25:28,750
The more he frowns, the scarier he looks.

531
00:25:29,270 --> 00:25:30,780
But I gave everything I had

532
00:25:30,950 --> 00:25:32,650
to start a conversation with him.

533
00:25:33,390 --> 00:25:34,160
Hello.

534
00:25:36,710 --> 00:25:37,540
I'm Jane.

535
00:25:38,080 --> 00:25:39,510
It's my first day here.

536
00:25:43,460 --> 00:25:44,250
I'm Jaab.

537
00:25:53,680 --> 00:25:55,930
The flea market opens at noon.

538
00:25:55,950 --> 00:25:57,360
Do you want to go together?

539
00:25:57,930 --> 00:25:59,200
I brought my own lunch.

540
00:25:59,510 --> 00:26:00,310
Oh.

541
00:26:00,790 --> 00:26:02,000
That's okay.

542
00:26:14,260 --> 00:26:15,210
Hello, Jane.

543
00:26:16,220 --> 00:26:16,780
Hi.

544
00:26:16,800 --> 00:26:17,440
Hi...

545
00:26:24,110 --> 00:26:24,840
I'm here...

546
00:26:25,150 --> 00:26:26,120
to get some apples.

547
00:26:26,230 --> 00:26:27,700
I found out later

548
00:26:27,720 --> 00:26:29,050
after talking to Min that

549
00:26:29,390 --> 00:26:32,310
the first impression Jaab put
so much effort into making

550
00:26:32,770 --> 00:26:35,270
was completely ruined by me.

551
00:26:39,150 --> 00:26:40,080
Hi, Jaab.

552
00:26:41,470 --> 00:26:42,160
Hello, Jane.

553
00:26:44,520 --> 00:26:46,030
And what happened next?

554
00:26:46,050 --> 00:26:48,000
How did you two become close?

555
00:26:49,310 --> 00:26:50,360
Mm...

556
00:26:50,570 --> 00:26:52,410
It was probably back when...

557
00:26:53,270 --> 00:26:54,910
I started a conversation with him.

558
00:26:54,930 --> 00:26:56,000
Wait for me, please.

559
00:26:57,990 --> 00:27:00,400
- Then it was just us in the same elevator.
- Hi, Jaab.

560
00:27:01,070 --> 00:27:02,080
Hello, Jane.

561
00:27:04,920 --> 00:27:05,530
And...

562
00:27:05,860 --> 00:27:08,470
- time didn't fly by too slowly there...
- Want some dough sticks?

563
00:27:09,990 --> 00:27:11,550
like it does whenever I'm with the others.

564
00:27:17,140 --> 00:27:17,890
Want some more?

565
00:27:21,710 --> 00:27:24,350
Before I knew it, we'd grown close.

566
00:27:26,160 --> 00:27:28,710
Did you tell Min about all of this?

567
00:27:29,450 --> 00:27:30,650
If she finds out,

568
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:31,850
I believe that

569
00:27:32,250 --> 00:27:34,280
she must be really happy for you.

570
00:27:35,720 --> 00:27:36,790
I've been busy,

571
00:27:37,160 --> 00:27:38,270
and so has she.

572
00:27:38,440 --> 00:27:39,960
So we haven't been in touch.

573
00:27:40,120 --> 00:27:41,950
And with Jaab...

574
00:27:42,710 --> 00:27:43,330
Well...

575
00:27:43,950 --> 00:27:45,750
We've been growing closer.

576
00:27:46,300 --> 00:27:49,390
We've gotten so used to each other that...

577
00:27:49,470 --> 00:27:50,480
there's no point in sharing.

578
00:27:51,980 --> 00:27:53,320
That's great.

579
00:27:55,870 --> 00:27:58,260
I've never imagined that

580
00:27:58,470 --> 00:28:00,880
I'd have another close friend aside from Min.

581
00:28:03,890 --> 00:28:04,440
Alright.

582
00:28:04,460 --> 00:28:05,750
Now that you're lying down,

583
00:28:05,780 --> 00:28:07,220
I guess I have to feed you like this.

584
00:28:11,590 --> 00:28:12,290
Oh!

585
00:28:13,310 --> 00:28:14,680
As delicious as always.

586
00:28:14,770 --> 00:28:15,750
It's from the same mango tree.

587
00:28:15,770 --> 00:28:17,350
Why wouldn't it taste the same?

588
00:28:27,730 --> 00:28:28,320
Oh?

589
00:28:29,100 --> 00:28:29,870
Jane!

590
00:28:30,150 --> 00:28:31,080
What are you doing?!

591
00:28:31,420 --> 00:28:32,680
I'm on my way to watch the sunset.

592
00:28:32,810 --> 00:28:34,110
Oh, and where are you...

593
00:28:34,640 --> 00:28:36,040
taking the motorbike?

594
00:28:37,200 --> 00:28:38,100
Oh.

595
00:28:38,120 --> 00:28:40,000
It's old now, and it gets loud when it runs.

596
00:28:40,170 --> 00:28:41,840
I'm afraid the sound might disturb you
while you work.

597
00:28:41,860 --> 00:28:43,720
So I'll start the engine far away from here.

598
00:28:44,800 --> 00:28:45,720
Oh, really?

599
00:28:46,020 --> 00:28:46,600
And...

600
00:28:47,080 --> 00:28:48,920
Where are you watching the sunset?

601
00:28:49,450 --> 00:28:50,280
Around here somewhere.

602
00:28:50,430 --> 00:28:51,640
Dad never allows me to go far.

603
00:28:52,880 --> 00:28:53,880
You look like

604
00:28:54,030 --> 00:28:55,400
someone who can't ride a motorbike.

605
00:28:55,700 --> 00:28:56,750
Can you really?

606
00:29:01,210 --> 00:29:01,800
Jane!

607
00:29:02,000 --> 00:29:04,630
Let's go!

608
00:29:04,900 --> 00:29:06,680
Woo-hoo!

609
00:29:08,930 --> 00:29:09,640
Jane,

610
00:29:10,080 --> 00:29:11,880
your place is super stunning.

611
00:29:12,330 --> 00:29:13,670
- So is that spot.
- Whoa, Jane.

612
00:29:13,690 --> 00:29:14,570
There, there.

613
00:29:14,590 --> 00:29:15,600
I want to go there, Jane.

614
00:29:15,960 --> 00:29:16,850
Let's go.

615
00:29:43,090 --> 00:29:44,340
Jane, you're so mean.

616
00:29:46,250 --> 00:29:46,970
Me?

617
00:29:47,460 --> 00:29:48,320
How exactly?

618
00:29:50,380 --> 00:29:51,590
You know a place this stunning,

619
00:29:51,740 --> 00:29:53,050
but you kept it all to yourself.

620
00:29:53,810 --> 00:29:55,380
You've never asked if I wanted to tag along.

621
00:29:59,430 --> 00:30:00,890
When you work,

622
00:30:00,910 --> 00:30:02,640
you like to be alone

623
00:30:02,660 --> 00:30:05,040
quietly in an isolated corner.

624
00:30:07,030 --> 00:30:09,620
Oh, you do care!

625
00:30:09,850 --> 00:30:12,300
You remember everything about me.

626
00:30:13,500 --> 00:30:15,470
Bew knows that you're here at my place.

627
00:30:16,010 --> 00:30:18,660
If you returned empty-handed,

628
00:30:19,120 --> 00:30:20,850
she would probably scold me as well.

629
00:30:22,780 --> 00:30:23,890
Oh, Jane.

630
00:30:24,380 --> 00:30:25,450
You ruined the mood.

631
00:30:27,140 --> 00:30:27,980
By the way,

632
00:30:28,500 --> 00:30:29,570
is this your usual spot?

633
00:30:31,080 --> 00:30:31,660
Mm.

634
00:30:32,050 --> 00:30:34,250
I came here every day
before my university years.

635
00:30:34,940 --> 00:30:36,120
It was part of my routine.

636
00:30:39,730 --> 00:30:40,880
Tell me about it.

637
00:30:41,660 --> 00:30:42,250
Hm?

638
00:30:42,950 --> 00:30:43,610
Well...

639
00:30:44,120 --> 00:30:45,200
Tell me anything

640
00:30:46,310 --> 00:30:47,710
that happened before we met.

641
00:30:51,790 --> 00:30:54,200
I grew up with the farm
and the orchards here.

642
00:30:55,250 --> 00:30:57,430
I was homeschooled here, too.

643
00:30:59,400 --> 00:31:02,480
My first big community was at the university.

644
00:31:03,640 --> 00:31:04,520
Then...

645
00:31:05,070 --> 00:31:06,440
I found myself a close friend.

646
00:31:07,120 --> 00:31:08,160
Her name is Min.

647
00:31:09,310 --> 00:31:10,040
Min...

648
00:31:12,440 --> 00:31:15,600
The company is my second big community.

649
00:31:17,110 --> 00:31:18,590
And I found myself another close friend.

650
00:31:19,790 --> 00:31:21,330
His name is Jaab.

651
00:31:28,320 --> 00:31:29,620
It's my pleasure.

652
00:31:39,230 --> 00:31:41,590
His world is something unknown to me.

653
00:31:43,510 --> 00:31:45,490
However, it answers the question I had.

654
00:31:46,090 --> 00:31:48,300
What turned him into someone...

655
00:31:51,740 --> 00:31:53,840
who is like a part of the sky,

656
00:31:56,110 --> 00:31:57,210
the clouds,

657
00:31:58,740 --> 00:32:00,160
and the sunlight?

658
00:32:01,880 --> 00:32:04,010
It's something beautiful and warm,

659
00:32:09,940 --> 00:32:11,430
yet at the same time,

660
00:32:17,760 --> 00:32:18,780
there appears to be a fine line

661
00:32:18,800 --> 00:32:20,800
between the two of us.

662
00:32:23,610 --> 00:32:24,280
Oh!

663
00:32:25,720 --> 00:32:26,440
Jane.

664
00:32:27,770 --> 00:32:29,520
Stop it, Jane.

665
00:32:30,710 --> 00:32:31,590
Jane, Jane.

666
00:32:31,610 --> 00:32:32,540
Jane! Jane!

667
00:32:32,560 --> 00:32:33,300
No, no.

668
00:32:33,320 --> 00:32:34,320
Jane, please.

669
00:32:37,660 --> 00:32:38,390
Jane. Cut, cut.

670
00:32:38,410 --> 00:32:39,540
Cut, cut, cut.

671
00:32:39,800 --> 00:32:41,160
Cut, cut. No, please, Jane.

672
00:32:42,780 --> 00:32:44,240
Jane, take it easy.

673
00:32:44,260 --> 00:32:46,300
Jane, no, no.

674
00:32:47,070 --> 00:32:48,720
Jane, Jane, Jane!

675
00:32:50,330 --> 00:32:51,960
When the male lead is about to make a move,

676
00:32:52,710 --> 00:32:54,360
it's like he's always pushed back

677
00:32:55,050 --> 00:32:56,970
to the point where he starts wondering...

678
00:32:57,330 --> 00:32:59,280
whether he should stop or keep going.

679
00:32:59,300 --> 00:33:00,600
Mm...

680
00:33:00,710 --> 00:33:02,260
The idea itself sounds interesting.

681
00:33:02,280 --> 00:33:04,250
But are you sure that
you listened to the right song?

682
00:33:05,540 --> 00:33:07,740
The crux of the story is...

683
00:33:07,760 --> 00:33:09,110
a fallout of a relationship.

684
00:33:09,400 --> 00:33:11,760
It's not being lost in love.

685
00:33:13,740 --> 00:33:15,860
I'm out of the loop,

686
00:33:15,880 --> 00:33:17,200
but I can tell he's very invested.

687
00:33:17,620 --> 00:33:19,520
Is there anything you'd like to confess?

688
00:33:20,930 --> 00:33:21,580
Hm?

689
00:33:22,340 --> 00:33:23,160
No!

690
00:33:23,480 --> 00:33:24,080
Well...

691
00:33:24,420 --> 00:33:26,400
This is how I operate.

692
00:33:26,580 --> 00:33:27,850
It's method acting, you see.

693
00:33:27,970 --> 00:33:29,440
But you're the director,

694
00:33:29,460 --> 00:33:30,380
not an actor.

695
00:33:30,400 --> 00:33:32,080
Acting, my ass.

696
00:33:32,210 --> 00:33:33,250
Fine, fine.

697
00:33:34,080 --> 00:33:36,110
So my idea hasn't hit the mark.

698
00:33:36,920 --> 00:33:37,750
But...

699
00:33:37,910 --> 00:33:39,320
I've still got time.

700
00:33:39,420 --> 00:33:40,740
Let me take some time to rethink.

701
00:33:40,760 --> 00:33:41,480
And then what?

702
00:33:42,060 --> 00:33:43,760
Are you going to stop here or keep going?

703
00:33:45,230 --> 00:33:47,550
I don't know either, but...

704
00:33:48,450 --> 00:33:49,970
Oh, you bastards!

705
00:33:49,990 --> 00:33:51,770
Both of you are fuckers!

706
00:33:51,790 --> 00:33:53,410
- Fuck you!
- I'm a bastard,

707
00:33:53,430 --> 00:33:54,380
just like you.

708
00:33:54,400 --> 00:33:55,610
- That's why we're friends.
- Ugh...

709
00:33:55,630 --> 00:33:57,390
I'm the tiniest bastard here, then.

710
00:33:57,410 --> 00:33:58,720
Plus, I'm the most handsome one.

711
00:33:58,740 --> 00:33:59,720
So what, huh?

712
00:33:59,750 --> 00:34:00,680
So... Oh!

713
00:34:03,590 --> 00:34:05,640
The bites of the mosquitoes here
are a bit less painful than a tiger's.

714
00:34:13,570 --> 00:34:14,630
You're on your phone?

715
00:34:15,380 --> 00:34:16,520
I'm sorry. I didn't notice.

716
00:34:16,770 --> 00:34:17,500
Oh.

717
00:34:18,060 --> 00:34:19,320
It's okay, Jane...

718
00:34:19,440 --> 00:34:20,320
By the way...

719
00:34:21,230 --> 00:34:22,550
How did you know that?

720
00:34:22,990 --> 00:34:24,120
Have you been bitten by a tiger before?

721
00:34:29,550 --> 00:34:30,850
Hey, Jane.

722
00:34:31,730 --> 00:34:33,320
Did I upset you in some way?

723
00:34:35,780 --> 00:34:37,120
The tiger wouldn't dare bite me.

724
00:34:38,350 --> 00:34:39,840
But it once broke into the orchard.

725
00:34:40,080 --> 00:34:41,010
What?!

726
00:34:41,580 --> 00:34:42,820
- I'm serious.
- Where, Jane?

727
00:34:43,340 --> 00:34:44,360
I saw it with my own eyes.

728
00:34:44,600 --> 00:34:45,840
It was gigantic.

729
00:34:46,580 --> 00:34:48,090
It was very intimidating, too.

730
00:34:49,030 --> 00:34:50,240
And it was...

731
00:34:50,280 --> 00:34:51,160
What?

732
00:34:52,900 --> 00:34:54,760
It was bouncing around on its tail.

733
00:34:54,920 --> 00:34:56,090
Was it, Jane?!

734
00:34:56,640 --> 00:34:57,420
And...

735
00:34:58,330 --> 00:35:00,100
the tiger was friends with a yellow bear

736
00:35:00,590 --> 00:35:01,840
and a pink piglet.

737
00:35:02,180 --> 00:35:03,000
Am I right?

738
00:35:04,000 --> 00:35:05,160
The tiger you're talking about...

739
00:35:06,310 --> 00:35:07,060
Ow!

740
00:35:08,610 --> 00:35:09,980
Are you teasing me?

741
00:35:10,000 --> 00:35:12,470
- Are you, Jane?
- Ow, you're squeezing my cheeks again.

742
00:35:12,490 --> 00:35:13,550
Oh, so what?

743
00:35:14,810 --> 00:35:15,920
- Take that.
- Ow, ow.

744
00:35:16,890 --> 00:35:18,020
What are you doing, Jane?

745
00:35:23,100 --> 00:35:23,880
I'm squeezing yours.

746
00:35:23,900 --> 00:35:24,880
There, there, there.

747
00:35:24,920 --> 00:35:26,730
I want to know what makes it fun,

748
00:35:26,750 --> 00:35:28,160
and why you like squeezing
my cheeks so much.

749
00:35:28,340 --> 00:35:29,240
Come on, then.

750
00:35:29,320 --> 00:35:29,960
Then...

751
00:35:30,100 --> 00:35:32,080
Whoever lets go first loses. Deal?

752
00:35:32,100 --> 00:35:33,240
Okay.

753
00:35:33,280 --> 00:35:34,060
Come on.

754
00:35:45,900 --> 00:35:47,620
- Come here. Come here.
- Bring it on.

755
00:36:05,270 --> 00:36:05,930
Jane.

756
00:36:10,890 --> 00:36:11,650
I...

757
00:36:14,440 --> 00:36:15,790
like...

758
00:36:16,540 --> 00:36:17,820
Dinner is ready, dear.

759
00:36:17,840 --> 00:36:19,730
The stir-fried chayote is nice and hot.

760
00:36:19,750 --> 00:36:21,400
stir-fried chayote very much!

761
00:36:25,580 --> 00:36:26,360
Really?

762
00:36:27,880 --> 00:36:29,880
You like stir-fried chayote?

763
00:36:30,220 --> 00:36:31,960
Do you know that chayote

764
00:36:31,980 --> 00:36:33,040
is my favorite?

765
00:36:33,540 --> 00:36:35,880
Auntie Kaew makes the best stir-fried chayote.

766
00:36:36,890 --> 00:36:38,280
I want you to try.

767
00:36:38,340 --> 00:36:39,010
Shall we?

768
00:36:39,330 --> 00:36:39,930
Mm.

769
00:36:40,270 --> 00:36:40,770
Come on.

770
00:36:41,780 --> 00:36:42,560
Let's go.

771
00:36:51,120 --> 00:36:52,760
What the hell is stir-fried chayote?

772
00:36:53,990 --> 00:36:55,190
Damn it, Jaab.

773
00:36:55,210 --> 00:36:56,620
You fucking idiot!

774
00:36:56,640 --> 00:36:59,160
- Jaab, are you coming or not?
- I am!

775
00:37:04,310 --> 00:37:05,920
Here you go.

776
00:37:06,640 --> 00:37:08,590
Here, stir-fried chayote.

777
00:37:09,280 --> 00:37:11,390
I kept the food pretty mild.

778
00:37:11,410 --> 00:37:13,760
I didn't know how much chili you could handle.

779
00:37:17,420 --> 00:37:18,080
Oh...

780
00:37:19,730 --> 00:37:21,620
A little spicy is fine, Auntie Kaew.

781
00:37:22,600 --> 00:37:23,980
Perfect. Well then...

782
00:37:24,000 --> 00:37:25,980
please go take a shower
right after you're finished,

783
00:37:26,000 --> 00:37:27,520
because it gets very cold late at night.

784
00:37:27,930 --> 00:37:29,720
Then come have some chilled longan in syrup.

785
00:37:29,790 --> 00:37:30,700
I made some for you.

786
00:37:30,720 --> 00:37:32,240
It's in the fridge, very chilled.

787
00:37:32,410 --> 00:37:33,460
Oh, Auntie Kaew.

788
00:37:33,820 --> 00:37:34,840
Thank you very much!

789
00:37:35,720 --> 00:37:37,560
Eat well. Enjoy.

790
00:37:37,580 --> 00:37:38,320
Thank you.

791
00:37:41,770 --> 00:37:43,440
Some stir-fried chayote for you.

792
00:37:43,870 --> 00:37:44,840
Eat up,

793
00:37:45,060 --> 00:37:45,820
Master Jaab.

794
00:37:46,860 --> 00:37:48,540
I'm not a kid, alright?

795
00:37:51,400 --> 00:37:52,170
Whoa!

796
00:37:55,290 --> 00:37:56,600
This is incredible, Jane.

797
00:38:00,680 --> 00:38:01,800
They are all incredible.

798
00:38:02,170 --> 00:38:03,050
Whoa...

799
00:38:06,960 --> 00:38:07,980
What are you looking at, Master Jane?

800
00:38:09,120 --> 00:38:10,480
Jaab, you chubby kid.

801
00:38:10,920 --> 00:38:11,550
What?

802
00:38:12,600 --> 00:38:14,090
Don't take a shot at me

803
00:38:14,590 --> 00:38:16,240
if you haven't seen my six-pack.

804
00:39:20,600 --> 00:39:21,400
Oh!

805
00:39:35,560 --> 00:39:37,560
[SCENE 1: INT. GARDEN HOUSE - DAY]
[CHARACTERS: CUTE]

806
00:39:37,650 --> 00:39:38,120
Whoa.

807
00:39:39,420 --> 00:39:40,590
What the fuck did I just type?

808
00:39:42,960 --> 00:39:44,840
You've totally lost it, Jaab...

809
00:39:50,700 --> 00:39:53,880
[JANE would like to share a photo]

810
00:39:58,930 --> 00:40:00,040
[Accept]

811
00:40:00,060 --> 00:40:00,900
What is it?

812
00:40:01,600 --> 00:40:02,680
[Open Gallery]

813
00:40:20,640 --> 00:40:21,500
Oh.

814
00:40:23,130 --> 00:40:24,210
Where?

815
00:40:26,440 --> 00:40:28,560
You came...?

816
00:40:29,380 --> 00:40:31,200
Finally...

817
00:40:33,400 --> 00:40:35,640
- Boo!
- Ah!

818
00:40:36,310 --> 00:40:37,420
Jane!

819
00:40:37,980 --> 00:40:38,920
What is this?

820
00:40:39,640 --> 00:40:40,890
You scared me.

821
00:40:43,400 --> 00:40:44,870
You almost gave me a heart attack.

822
00:40:50,430 --> 00:40:52,530
You invited me out for stargazing
by sending me a photo?

823
00:40:52,610 --> 00:40:53,770
What if I missed the notification?

824
00:40:55,090 --> 00:40:56,440
I was afraid that you'd already gone to bed.

825
00:40:56,860 --> 00:40:58,240
So I decided to send a photo.

826
00:40:58,900 --> 00:41:00,480
If your AirDrop was on,

827
00:41:00,500 --> 00:41:02,840
then your laptop would be on, too.

828
00:41:03,140 --> 00:41:05,060
Which would mean that you were still up.

829
00:41:05,800 --> 00:41:06,570
Jane.

830
00:41:06,860 --> 00:41:07,990
Don't complicate things.

831
00:41:08,340 --> 00:41:09,720
Just ask me if you want.

832
00:41:10,050 --> 00:41:12,840
Even if I were asleep,
I would wake up for you.

833
00:41:19,270 --> 00:41:20,570
The stars here are beautiful,

834
00:41:21,360 --> 00:41:22,820
in case you want to put them in the MV.

835
00:41:31,790 --> 00:41:32,570
Whoa!

836
00:41:32,970 --> 00:41:34,080
You're right!

837
00:41:37,870 --> 00:41:39,060
Jaab, lie down.

838
00:41:39,160 --> 00:41:40,380
It's like looking at a giant TV screen.

839
00:41:40,490 --> 00:41:41,060
Huh?

840
00:41:41,120 --> 00:41:41,980
Come on.

841
00:41:44,400 --> 00:41:44,920
Oh.

842
00:41:51,040 --> 00:41:52,400
Whoa.

843
00:41:55,620 --> 00:41:56,310
Jaab.

844
00:41:56,800 --> 00:41:57,470
Hm?

845
00:41:58,490 --> 00:42:00,690
Have you ever stargazed
in a classroom before?

846
00:42:02,650 --> 00:42:04,070
How could that be possible, Jane?

847
00:42:04,280 --> 00:42:05,840
A classroom comes with a ceiling.

848
00:42:08,060 --> 00:42:08,840
But here,

849
00:42:10,210 --> 00:42:11,570
you're doing it right now.

850
00:42:12,800 --> 00:42:14,020
This used to be my classroom.

851
00:42:17,290 --> 00:42:18,280
You mean...

852
00:42:18,670 --> 00:42:20,300
back when you were homeschooled?

853
00:42:20,590 --> 00:42:21,130
Mm.

854
00:42:21,830 --> 00:42:22,840
I studied here,

855
00:42:23,390 --> 00:42:25,040
had lunches here,

856
00:42:25,470 --> 00:42:26,590
and played here.

857
00:42:26,800 --> 00:42:28,310
I spent all my time here.

858
00:42:33,400 --> 00:42:34,220
So...

859
00:42:34,770 --> 00:42:36,180
why were you homeschooled?

860
00:42:36,800 --> 00:42:38,300
Out of everyone I know,

861
00:42:38,330 --> 00:42:39,920
you're the first.

862
00:42:42,660 --> 00:42:44,610
I went to a regular school when I was little.

863
00:42:45,330 --> 00:42:47,370
But I was small, so I was always picked on.

864
00:42:48,750 --> 00:42:50,710
I cried on the way home every day.

865
00:42:51,520 --> 00:42:52,820
My parents were worried about me,

866
00:42:53,620 --> 00:42:56,440
so they wanted me to do
whatever made me happy.

867
00:42:57,700 --> 00:42:59,200
And what made me happy

868
00:42:59,810 --> 00:43:00,840
was staying home.

869
00:43:02,660 --> 00:43:03,390
That's why

870
00:43:03,650 --> 00:43:05,140
I was homeschooled.

871
00:43:08,580 --> 00:43:09,940
So your classroom

872
00:43:10,590 --> 00:43:12,940
has the most beautiful view ever, huh?

873
00:43:14,440 --> 00:43:15,080
Yeah.

874
00:43:36,500 --> 00:43:37,260
Jaab...

875
00:43:40,820 --> 00:43:41,640
Jane...

876
00:43:51,300 --> 00:43:52,620
I...

877
00:43:59,240 --> 00:44:00,500
like you.

878
00:44:02,640 --> 00:44:04,240
I like you, too.

879
00:44:41,800 --> 00:44:43,430
Your classroom

880
00:44:44,080 --> 00:44:46,600
is probably the most beautiful
one in the world, yeah?

881
00:44:47,840 --> 00:44:48,440
Mm.

882
00:44:52,740 --> 00:44:53,440
I also...

883
00:44:53,600 --> 00:44:54,920
said the same thing

884
00:44:55,540 --> 00:44:57,710
when I was talking to Min.

885
00:45:15,850 --> 00:45:16,600
Ow!

886
00:45:17,520 --> 00:45:18,200
Jane!

887
00:45:18,290 --> 00:45:19,160
What did you do?!

888
00:45:19,440 --> 00:45:20,350
I'm sorry.

889
00:45:20,940 --> 00:45:21,810
There was a mosquito.

890
00:45:24,250 --> 00:45:27,110
I swear I was being as gentle as I could.

891
00:45:29,430 --> 00:45:30,200
Did it hurt?

892
00:45:30,680 --> 00:45:31,500
Hold on.

893
00:45:32,380 --> 00:45:33,480
What happened?

894
00:45:33,660 --> 00:45:35,230
Did I fall asleep?

895
00:45:35,660 --> 00:45:36,200
Mm.

896
00:45:37,870 --> 00:45:38,560
And...

897
00:45:38,750 --> 00:45:39,720
How long was I asleep?

898
00:45:41,580 --> 00:45:42,720
A while.

899
00:45:43,440 --> 00:45:44,470
And...

900
00:45:44,520 --> 00:45:46,320
While I was asleep,

901
00:45:46,340 --> 00:45:48,020
did I do something strange?

902
00:45:49,230 --> 00:45:51,040
Tell me the truth. I won't get mad.

903
00:45:53,880 --> 00:45:54,640
Nothing.

904
00:45:55,400 --> 00:45:56,040
Really?

905
00:45:56,780 --> 00:45:57,470
Mm.

906
00:46:10,030 --> 00:46:11,230
Your life here is so comfortable.

907
00:46:11,250 --> 00:46:13,240
Why did you move to Bangkok
to work for someone else?

908
00:46:13,260 --> 00:46:14,200
I just wanted to see

909
00:46:14,390 --> 00:46:16,840
what a starless night sky looked like.

910
00:46:17,030 --> 00:46:17,710
I think...

911
00:46:17,960 --> 00:46:19,440
I'm gonna make a move on Jane.

912
00:46:19,460 --> 00:46:20,440
Jaab has a crush on...

913
00:46:20,490 --> 00:46:21,470
- Hey, wait, wait.
- Hey, hey!

914
00:46:21,490 --> 00:46:22,960
Oh, I...

915
00:46:23,160 --> 00:46:24,330
Spending time with you

916
00:46:24,480 --> 00:46:26,280
makes my life seem a lot simpler.

917
00:46:26,300 --> 00:46:27,800
Stay with me for a long time, okay?

918
00:46:27,970 --> 00:46:29,040
Don't leave.

919
00:46:29,160 --> 00:46:31,330
If you don't tell me to leave,
then I won't.

920
00:46:31,880 --> 00:46:33,340
Are you...

921
00:46:33,400 --> 00:46:35,800
having a crush on someone?

922
00:46:36,000 --> 00:46:37,220
Is it me?!
